Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:52:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 48/52] serve: picture age-out is opt-in
 (STRATA_IMAGE_HISTORY=tools|<N>), keeps a prefill's pictures, logs what it
 did

AGENTS.md: a new feature is opt-in. Unset (or keep/0) every picture stays, as in the last release. "tools" turns
pictures a tool returned in answered turns into a note; "<N>" also a picture in the user message right after tool
results and every user picture N assistant turns old (an agent session that starts with screenshots made every turn
run alone without the per-slot M-RoPE regions). A trailing assistant message (prefill) no longer counts as an answer,
nothing is aged without an encoder, and the image-request line counts the prompt with its picture rows, lists at
most 8 messages and says how many pictures were left out. Tests on the OpenAI, Anthropic and Responses paths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
